  "adaptations": [
    "Entry resolves actual professional skill sources instead of sibling bundled snapshots.",
    "Read-only bounded detector with externally observed host/task evidence and task-specific readiness.",
    "ETF style selection always uses an explicit approved library or public synthetic examples.",
    "Local reader integration and independent DataLab runtime validated against synthetic sources only.",
    "Persistent per-machine setup with source/runtime drift detection.",
    "Explicit scoped feedback and reviewed personal/project memory with expiry, supersession, rollback and deletion.",
    "Real local plugin installation, native discovery in a fresh CLI session, and held-out memory-guided synthetic task.",
    "Pin LF endings across Git checkouts so Windows autocrlf cannot invalidate exact-byte fingerprints.",
    "Rename project, marketplace, plugin and skill to DF Agent / df-agent; preserve durable schemas and existing local state with legacy default fallback.",
    "Five collaboration rules: align before long outputs, concise conclusions, surgical revisions, verifiable delivery and source read-only handling.",
    "Task-scoped write grants for setup, output, memory, feedback and runtime; N:/digital finance remains a protected source root.",
    "Per-user runtime indexes/cache/logs/tmp outside sources; memory reads no longer create lock files; Windows concurrent snapshot handling is bounded.",
    "Router/Advisor delegates source catalog, indexing, retrieval and technical acceptance to df-mcp and computation to DataLab.",
    "Bounded reader manifest/core/vendor drift checks and CSV/TSV/XLSX-specific dependency evidence; unknown readiness remains explicit.",
    "Optional native source catalog/evidence-envelope consumption preserves raw errors, extraction freshness and business-completeness limits."
  ],
